# Double-click takes a word, triple-click takes the line.
#
# The band itself is a drawn rectangle and invisible to a text assertion, so
# the composer's "N selected" readout is what makes the selection observable —
# which is also why it exists: a short highlight behind text is easy to miss.
#
# env: HANABI_SELECT_AUDIT=1
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

expect_no_text selected

# Inside "ledger" on the first account line: six characters, and the line
# itself is 61.
#
# THE Y IS A LINE CENTRE AND NOTHING ELSE WILL DO. 234 / 250 / 266 are the
# element TOPS, not centres -- each line's element is 16px tall, so the first
# account line is 218..234 and 234 is the seam it shares with the second. A
# press on a seam used to land in both (see
# a_click_on_a_line_seam_is_one_click.e2e); it now lands in the lower one, and
# 250 selected the SECOND account line -- 58 characters, not 61. That is what
# this test was failing on, deterministically, on a clean tree: the count in
# the assertion belongs to a line the coordinate stopped pointing at.
#
# 226 is the centre of 218..234, eight pixels from either edge.
#
# RE-MEASURE IT MECHANICALLY. HANABI_SELECT_AUDIT=1 prints, for every press,
# the element it landed in, its rect, its length and its first characters:
#
#   [sel] press=(415.0,226.0) run=1 off=17 rect=(329.0,218.0 656.0x16.0)
#         len=61 text="  acct 8842 - ledger $128.60, computed $116.20 ..."
#
# That is the line, the count and the point in one line of a normal run.
# Rendering the thread and scanning the PNG is what this cost last time.
#
# The history of the number, kept because it says how often this moves: the
# three body lines sit at 218 / 234 / 250 as element tops. They were at 209 / 225 / 241 until the
# transcript's own spacing was re-derived against Puffin's source (turn air
# 9+6+9 and a 12px top inset, feat/vis-pane), which put every reply 9px lower.
# They were at 226 / 242 / 258 before that, until the hover
# Copy row stopped being reserved in the layout (feat/vis-fixture: it is an
# overlay on the bubble now, as Puffin's is), which lifted every reply by 24px
# and then put 10 back as turn air and 4 as the transcript's top inset. They
# were at 184 / 200 / 216 before that, until the thread began on a user turn (a
# right-aligned bubble and its avatar, to match Puffin's reference frame). A
# coordinate click is brittle by nature (see afterhours_gaps.md: there is no
# way to ask where a piece of text landed), so if this starts selecting the
# wrong word, re-measure rather than nudge -- render t2 at this script's own
# 1100x760 and scan the PNG for the bubble's band.
double_click 415 226
wait_frames 6
expect_text "6 selected"

# The whole line is much longer than one word.
triple_click 415 226
wait_frames 6
expect_no_text "6 selected"
expect_text "61 selected"

# A press on empty space drops it.
click 700 300
wait_frames 6
expect_no_text selected
